  "p": "The Re_h = 100 run of seed 21 had the lowest held-out loss of the 30/90 runs and the largest argmin error; the only run that met the convergence definition (30/90, Re_h 100, seed 23) has the largest velocity error of the 30/90 runs. Every other run was still improving when the fixed schedule ended."
 },
 {
  "h2": "6.2 30/120 and run 5"
 },
 {
  "p": "For 30/120 J rises across [0.35, 0.65] at Re_h 0.1, 1 and 10, and below the range it falls until the geometry refuses the split at s = 0.268. Runs 6 and 7 therefore end on the range's bound with the reference, and test drop and field accuracy only. Run 5 (Re_h 0.1) was stopped at LM step ~100 for that reason and recorded as skipped. Run 8 (Re_h 100) has an interior optimum and is the one 30/120 test of the argmin: the PINN put it at 0.3998 against 0.3859, regret 0.080%."
